[38;5;231m⏺[39m No second form yet. That's important — it means YAGNI is the main design risk here: the cheapest way to get this wrong
  is to invent a rule vocabulary for forms nobody has specified.

  [1mThe fork:[0m how much validation capability to build now, before any second form exists to constrain it. This one is not
  cheap to change later in one respect — the [3mcall signature[0m and the [3merror shape[0m become an interface the login form and
  every future form depend on. The set of rules behind that interface, by contrast, is cheap to grow.

  - [1mMinimal engine, one rule[0m — a [38;5;153mvalidate(values, rules)[39m that walks a declarative field→rules map and returns per-field
    errors, shipping only [38;5;153mrequired[39m. Buys you the seam and the error shape now; costs almost nothing; rules out nothing,
    since adding [38;5;153mminLength[39m/[38;5;153memail[39m later is additive. Only real cost: the next form's author writes the rule they need
    instead of finding it ready.
  - [1mEngine plus a starter rule library[0m — same engine, but [38;5;153mrequired[39m, [38;5;153mminLength[39m, [38;5;153mmaxLength[39m, [38;5;153memail[39m, [38;5;153mpattern[39m, and custom
    predicates ship immediately. Buys readiness; costs untested-by-real-use code and message wording guessed in advance.
    Rules out nothing either, but wrong guesses tend to get worked around rather than fixed.
  - [1mAdopt a validation library[0m (zod, yup, valibot) — buys a mature vocabulary; costs a build step this repo doesn't
    have. [38;5;153mapp.js[39m is loaded by a bare [38;5;153m<script>[39m tag with no bundler and no [38;5;153mdependencies[39m in [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m. Hard to undo
    relative to the others.

  [1mMy recommendation: the minimal engine with one rule.[0m The valuable, hard-to-change part is the seam and the error
  shape, and you get both. With zero known second forms, every rule beyond [38;5;153mrequired[39m is speculation, and a library is a
  disproportionate infrastructure commitment for a 28-line [38;5;153mapp.js[39m.
