[1m[38;5;231mHow much validation capability should ship in this change?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mMinimal engine, required only (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mDeclarative field→rules map, per-field error results, only the `required` rule implemented. Adding rules later is [39m
     [38;5;246madditive and cheap.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Engine + starter rule library
     [38;5;246mAlso ship minLength, maxLength, email, pattern, and custom predicates now, with default messages, so future forms [39m
     [38;5;246mhave them ready.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Adopt a validation library
     [38;5;246mUse zod/yup/valibot. Requires introducing npm dependencies and a bundler or import-map — neither exists in this [39m
     [38;5;246mrepo today.[39m
